p=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M1.50562 7.94373H11.5342\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M1.73071 2.24432H16.3691\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M1.73071 13.6622H7.77047\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</svg>\n</span> Notes</a></div>\n  <div class=\"wprm-layout-column-container wprm-column-gap-40 wprm-column-rows-recipe-900 meadow-main-columns\">\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-left\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-5892-ingredients\" class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-5892-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before\" data-recipe=\"5892\" data-servings=\"8\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Ingredients<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-ingredients wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Fruits</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">6</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cups</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">peeled and sliced apples</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">your favorite variety, such as Granny Smith or Fuji</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Caramel</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">14 oz bag</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">soft caramel candies</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">or substitute with ¾ cup caramel sauce</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Cake Mix</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">box (15.25 oz)</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">yellow cake mix</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">any brand will do</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">unsalted butter</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">that’s 2 sticks, melted</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">½</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">ground cinnamon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a warm, spicy kick</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">pinch</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">enhances the flavors</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-5892-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"5892\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 9&#215;13-inch baking dish&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">Greased for easy removal</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Mixing bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing ingredients if needed</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-5892-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-5892-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"5892\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5892-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Preheat your oven to 350°F. This ensures your cake bakes evenly and comes out perfectly golden.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5892-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Grease a 9&#215;13-inch baking dish. This will help prevent the cake from sticking and make cleanup a breeze.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5892-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Arrange apple slices evenly in the greased dish. Sprinkle them with a dash of cinnamon and a pinch of salt for extra flavor.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5892-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Drizzle caramel sauce or melted caramels over the apples. This will create a deliciously gooey layer.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5892-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Evenly pour the dry cake mix over the caramel-coated apples. No need to mix; just let it sit on top!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5892-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Drizzle melted butter over the top layer of cake mix. This will help it brown beautifully while baking.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5892-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Bake for 45–50 minutes until the top is golden brown and the caramel is bubbly. Your kitchen will smell amazing!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5892-step-0-7\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Let the cake cool for 10 minutes before serving. Optionally, serve with vanilla ice cream or whipped cream for a delightful finish.</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-5892-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>350</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>3g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>55g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sugar</td>\n<td>30g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here&#8217;s everything you need to make a delicious caramel apple dump cake!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ingredients-for-Caramel-Apple-Dump-Cake.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for caramel apple dump cake displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-5890\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ingredients-for-Caramel-Apple-Dump-Cake.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ingredients-for-Caramel-Apple-Dump-Cake-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>6 cups peeled and sliced apples</strong> – your favorite variety, such as Granny Smith or Fuji</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 (14 oz) bag of soft caramel candies</strong> – or substitute with ¾ cup caramel sauce</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 box yellow cake mix (15.25 oz)</strong> – any brand will do</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup unsalted butter</strong> – that’s 2 sticks, melted</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>½ teaspoon ground cinnamon</strong> – for a warm, spicy kick</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>pinch of salt</strong> – enhances the flavors</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-caramel-apple-dump-cake\"><strong>How to Make caramel apple dump cake</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delightful caramel apple <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dump_cake\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">dump cake</a> is a breeze to make! With a preparation time of just 15 minutes and a cooking time of 45–50 minutes, you’ll have a warm, gooey dessert ready to enjoy in no time. Allow it to cool for 10 minutes before serving, and consider pairing it with a scoop of vanilla ice cream or a dollop of whipped cream for an extra treat!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Step-by-Step-Caramel-Apple-Dump-Cake-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step preparation of caramel apple dump cake, including greasing the dish, arranging apples, drizzling caramel, and pouring cake mix.\" class=\"wp-image-5891\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Step-by-Step-Caramel-Apple-Dump-Cake-Preparation.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Step-by-Step-Caramel-Apple-Dump-Cake-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat your oven to 350°F. This ensures your cake bakes evenly and comes out perfectly golden.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Prepare the Baking Dish</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Grease a 9&#215;13-inch baking dish. This will help prevent the cake from sticking and make cleanup a breeze.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Arrange the Apples</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Arrange apple slices evenly in the greased dish. Sprinkle them with a dash of cinnamon and a pinch of salt for extra flavor.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Add the Caramel</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Drizzle caramel sauce or melted caramels over the apples. This will create a deliciously gooey layer.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Pour the Cake Mix</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Evenly pour the dry cake mix over the caramel-coated apples. No need to mix; just let it sit on top!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Drizzle with Butter</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Drizzle melted butter over the top layer of cake mix. This will help it brown beautifully while baking.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Bake the Cake</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bake for 45–50 minutes until the top is golden brown and the caramel is bubbly. Your kitchen will smell amazing!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 8: Cool and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Let the cake cool for 10 minutes before serving. Optionally, serve with vanilla ice cream or whipped cream for a delightful finish.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Dessert</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>50 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>10 minutes (resting)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>75 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm with ice cream or whipped cream!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-caramel-apple-dump-cake\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making caramel apple dump cake</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Opt for tart apples like Granny Smith for a balanced flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drizzle extra caramel sauce on top for a decadent finish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a mix of cake flavors for a unique twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let it cool slightly before serving to enhance the flavors.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with vanilla ice cream for a delightful contrast.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-caramel-apple-dump-cake\"><strong>How to Serve this caramel apple dump cake</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Top with a scoop of vanilla ice cream for a creamy contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drizzle extra caramel sauce over each slice for added sweetness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve warm with a dollop of whipped cream for a delightful finish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a cup of hot apple cider for a cozy autumn treat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a sprinkle of cinnamon for an extra flavor boost.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a side of fresh apple slices for a refreshing crunch.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can make this cake ahead and store it easily:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow the cake to cool completely.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cover it tightly with plastic wrap or aluminum foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For best results, keep it in an airtight container.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool the cake completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap it tightly in plastic wrap, then in aluminum foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 3 months.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight before serving.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place the cake in an oven-safe dish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cover with foil to prevent over-browning.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat for about 15-20 minutes or until warmed through.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is the biggest mistake to avoid when making a dump cake?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>One of the biggest mistakes to avoid when making a dump cake is not layering the ingredients properly. Make sure to spread the fruit evenly on the bottom and sprinkle the cake mix on top without mixing. This ensures that the cake bakes evenly and the flavors meld beautifully. Also, avoid using too much butter, as it can make the cake overly greasy instead of moist and delicious.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What are the ingredients in caramel apple dump cake?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The ingredients for caramel apple dump cake are quite simple and include sliced apples (fresh or canned), caramel sauce, a box of yellow cake mix, and butter. You can also add cinnamon for extra flavor. This combination creates a delightful dessert that’s easy to prepare and perfect for any occasion.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What is the best apple for apple dump cake?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The best apples for caramel apple dump cake are those that hold their shape well during baking. Varieties like Granny Smith, Honeycrisp, or Fuji are excellent choices. They provide a nice balance of sweetness and tartness, which complements the caramel beautifully and adds depth to the flavor of the cake.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Does caramel apple dump cake need to be refrigerated?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Caramel apple dump cake can be stored at room temperature for a couple of days, but it’s best to refrigerate it if you want to keep it fresh for longer. Make sure to cover it with plastic wrap or store it in an airtight container. This will help maintain its deliciousness and prevent it from drying out. Enjoy it warm or cold, as both are delightful!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">As you dive into this delightful caramel apple dump cake, remember the joy of simple pleasures! It’s a warm hug in dessert form, perfect for sharing with loved ones or savoring solo. So grab your ingredients, let the aromas fill your kitchen, and enjoy every gooey, sweet bite. You’ve earned this delicious treat!</p>\n",
